# Runtime core size budget: the most code lines elastos/crates/elastos-runtime may hold.
#
# scripts/core-size.py counts the crate as code only: no tests (the tests/ directory,
# modules declared only under a test cfg, and items behind one), no comment-only lines, no
# blank lines. The core-size CI job fails when the count is above this number, or more
# than 50 below it. The goal is a core of about 10,000 lines.
#
# To grow the core, raise this number in the same pull request as the code, so reviewers
# see the growth and decide on it. When the core shrinks more than 50 lines below the
# budget, the check fails until the same pull request lowers this number to the new
# count, so freed room cannot be spent again. Measure with: python3 scripts/core-size.py
9843
